    exchange_id: uint8 &convert=ExchangeId($$);
    root_symbol: bytes &size=6;
    contract_month_code: uint8 &convert=ContractMonthCode($$);
    expiry_year: bytes &size=2;
    expiry_day: bytes &size=2;
    call_put_code: uint8 &convert=CallPutCode($$);
    # Strike Price Instrument Fraction Pair is the same bytes whichever arm the model names: its arms lay them out alike and differ only in what they are called and what they mean, which Strike Price Fraction Indicator says (Strike Price Instrument Negative Whole Pair, Strike Price Instrument Negative Ten Pair, Strike Price Instrument Negative Hundred Pair, Strike Price Instrument Negative Thousand Pair, Strike Price Instrument Negative Ten Thousand Pair, Strike Price Instrument Negative Hundred Thousand Pair, Strike Price Instrument Negative Million Pair, Strike Price Instrument Numeric Pair). They are parsed as StrikePriceInstrumentNumericPair, so which arm applies is left to what is built on the definition.
